.TH FATHOM_NOTE 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-note \- The review memory: notes, decisions, questions and follow\-ups, committed under `.fathom/reviews/` (`e6.5`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom note\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The review memory: notes, decisions, questions and follow\-ups, committed under `.fathom/reviews/` (`e6.5`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the report as one JSON line on stdout (`fathom.cli.note/1`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fathom\-note\-add(1)
Record a note, decision, question or follow\-up against an episode or a path
.TP
fathom\-note\-list(1)
List what is recorded, oldest first
.TP
fathom\-note\-show(1)
Show one note with its evidence and its link verdict
.TP
fathom\-note\-answer(1)
Answer a question or close a follow\-up by appending the note that closes it
.TP
fathom\-note\-withdraw(1)
Take a recorded decision back, by appending the note that retracts it
.TP
fathom\-note\-verify(1)
Re\-hash every note against its own `digest:` line — tampering, and nothing else
